{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:regular-set","title":"def:regular-set","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1078,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:regular-set","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:regular-set","line":1694,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The regular set]\n\\label{def:regular-set}\n\n\n\n\nLet $M$ be a smooth manifold and $f\\colon M\\to\\mathbb R$ smooth. The\n\\emph{regular set} of $f$ is\n\\[\n\\mathcal R=\\{x\\in M:df_x\\ne0\\}.\n\\]\nIts points are \\emph{regular}; the remaining points are \\emph{critical}.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The regular set] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a726567756c61722d736574\"></span> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a smooth manifold and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$\">$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$</span> smooth. The <em>regular set</em> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\mathcal R=\\{ x\\in M:df_x\\ne 0\\} .  \\]\">\\[  \\mathcal R=\\{ x\\in M:df_x\\ne 0\\} .  \\]</span> Its points are <em>regular</em>; the remaining points are <em>critical</em>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:gradient-orthogonal-iff","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:regular-set-eq-gradient-nonvanishing","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:regular-set-eq-gradient-nonv